      ],\par
      "reflectionQuestions": [\par
        "When last did I intentionally express love in a meaningful way?",\par
        "Has familiarity replaced intentional affection?",\par
        "What does romance look like for my spouse now?"\par
      ],\par
      "practicalApplication": "Do one unexpected, thoughtful gesture today that communicates intentional affection to your spouse.",\par
      "challenge": "Do not wait for feelings\emdash create moments; romance must be cultivated, not assumed.",\par
      "prayer": "Lord, rekindle love and affection in our marriage. Deliver us from emotional neglect, teach us to express love intentionally, and let our connection grow richer. Amen."\par
    \},\par
    \{\par
      "date": "November 9, 2026",\par
      "title": "Aging Together Gracefully",\par
      "scripture": "Isaiah 46:4",\par
      "teaching": [\par
        "Aging introduces physical and energetic changes, but it offers couples the opportunity to build enduring, quiet companionship.",\par
        "Graceful aging requires accepting physical changes without insecurity and valuing presence over external appearance.",\par
        "Couples who age together gracefully cultivate a deep, knowing love that transcends the need for constant words.",\par
        "True commitment is revealed by consistently loving who your spouse was, who they are, and who they are becoming in decline.",\par
        "Building a mature love that outlives physical strength turns the home into a sanctuary of peace through life's final seasons."\par
      ],\par
      "illustration": [\par
