  \{\par
    "id": 42,\par
    "title": "Lesson 42: Financial Accountability and Kingdom Impact",\par
    "texts": [\par
      "Luke 16:10\f1\endash 13",\par
      "Matthew 25:14\endash 30",\par
      "Acts 4:32\endash 35",\par
      "2 Corinthians 9:6\endash 11"\par
    ],\par
    "lessonAim": \{\par
      "know": "Understand that financial success requires transparency and accountability to God",\par
      "believe": "Believe that Kingdom wealth is measured by impact and generosity rather than accumulation",\par
      "practice": "Maintain accurate records and prioritize funding the Gospel and helping the needy"\par
    \},\par
    "memoryVerse": \{\par
      "text": "Moreover it is required in stewards, that a man be found faithful.",\par
      "reference": "1 Corinthians 4:2 (KJV)"\par
    \},\par
    "introduction": [\par
      "Financial success without accountability is dangerous; it invites waste and pride. God is looking for faithful stewards who manage resources with integrity.",\par
      "True Kingdom wealth is measured by what flows *through* you to bless others. We must be accountable stewards who avoid waste to maximize Kingdom impact."\par
    ],\par
    "introQuestion": "If God audited your bank statement today, would He find a steward of His mission or a consumer of His blessings?",\par
    "exposition": \{\par
      "title": "a. Biblical Explanation (What the Text Means)",\par
      "sections": \{\par
        "title": "Biblical Explanation",\par
        "points": [\par
          \{\par
            "scripture": "Luke 16:10\endash 13",\par
            "explanation": [\par
              "Faithfulness in 'least' (money) is the test for being trusted with 'much' (spiritual authority)",\par
              "You cannot serve two masters; your management of money reveals your true loyalty"\par
            ]\par
          \},\par
          \{\par
            "scripture": "Acts 4:32\endash 35",\par
            "explanation": [\par
              "The Early Church model: United, accountable distribution ensured no one suffered lack",\par
              "Sacrificial giving is the engine of communal transformation and Kingdom expansion"\par
            ]\par
          \},\par
          \{\par
            "scripture": "Matthew 25:14\endash 30",\par
            "explanation": [\par
              "The Parable of the Talents teaches that accountability involves multiplication, not just preservation",\par
              "Fear and excuses are the enemies of faithful stewardship"\par
            ]\par
          \}\par
        ]\par
      \}\par
    \},\par
    "theologicalClarification": \{\par
      "title": "b. Theological Clarification (Avoiding Extremes)",\par
      "points": [\par
        "Accountability is both vertical (to God) and horizontal (to leadership/family/spouses).",\par
        "Kingdom Impact is not just 'giving to the church'\emdash it includes social justice, helping the poor, and ethical business.",\par
        "Waste is defined as using resources for things that do not align with God's stated priorities for your life."\par
      ]\par
    \},\par
    "doctrinalAlignment": \{\par
      "title": "c. Doctrinal Alignment",\par
      "points": [\par
        "The Judgment Seat of Christ: Every believer will give an account of their resource management",\par
        "The Body of Christ: Wealth is distributed within the body to ensure the needs of the mission are met",\par
        "Biblical Integrity: Financial honesty is a requirement for spiritual leadership"\par
      ]\par
    \},\par
    "keyTruths": [\par
      "Accountability prevents the 'luxury addiction' that stalls spiritual growth",\par
      "Accurate record-keeping is a spiritual discipline",\par
      "Giving transforms lives and attracts thanksgiving to God",\par
      "Stewardship is a preparation for eternal responsibility",\par
      "Integrity in finances is a powerful witness to the world"\par
    ],\par
    "lifeApplication": [\par
      \{ "category": "Transparency", "instruction": "If married, hold a 'Family Finance Night' to review all accounts, tithes, and goals openly" \},\par
      \{ "category": "Tracking", "instruction": "Use a budget app or notebook to track every transaction this week for 100% accountability" \},\par
      \{ "category": "Kingdom Seed", "instruction": "Make a specific giving commitment today toward a mission project or a family in crisis" \},\par
      \{ "category": "Youth/Habit", "instruction": "Children and youth should start a 'Give, Save, Spend' jar system to learn prioritization early" \},\par
      \{ "category": "Prayer", "instruction": "Daily ask: 'Lord, what portion of this income is for me, and what portion is for Your Kingdom?'" \}\par
    ],\par
    "discussionQuestions": [\par
      "What systems can you use to track and manage your money better?",\par
      "How does your giving determine the scale of your Kingdom impact?",\par
      "Why does God test our character with money before giving us spiritual power?"\par
    ],\par
    "caseStudy": \{\par
      "scenario": "A successful business owner gives large donations to the church but hides high-interest debts and shady business deals from their family.",\par
      "questions": [\par
        "Is this person being 'found faithful' according to 1 Corinthians 4:2?",\par
        "How does 'hidden' financial dealing affect their spiritual authority?"\par
      ]\par
    \},\par
    "personalReflection": [\par
      "Do I spend to impress people or to express God's purpose?",\par
      "Am I a funnel for God's blessings or a reservoir that keeps it all?",\par
      "Is my financial integrity above reproach?"\par
    ],\par
    "actionPoint": "Identify one 'wasteful' expense in your budget and redirect that specific amount to a Kingdom cause this month."\par
  \},\par
  \par
  \{\par
    "id": 43,\par
    "title": "Lesson 43: Understanding Divine Purpose",\par
    "texts": [\par
      "Jeremiah 1:4\endash 10",\par
      "Ephesians 2:10",\par
      "Romans 8:28\endash 30",\par
      "2 Timothy 1:9"\par
    ],\par
    "lessonAim": \{\par
      "know": "Identify divine purpose as God's original intention that precedes human birth",\par
      "believe": "Believe that fulfillment is found only in discovering and aligning with God's tailored plan",\par
      "practice": "Pursue an intimate walk with God to discern specific gifts, passions, and assignments"\par
    \},\par
    "memoryVerse": \{\par
      "text": "The counsel of the Lord standeth forever, the thoughts of His heart to all generations.",\par
      "reference": "Psalm 33:11 (KJV)"\par
    \},\par
    "introduction": [\par
      "Before you were born, God already had a plan. You are not an accident; you are a product of divine intention.",\par
      "Purpose is the 'Why' behind your existence. Many struggle not from lack of talent, but from lack of alignment with God's original design."\par
    ],\par
    "introQuestion": "Are you living a purpose-driven life or a survival-driven life?",\par
    "exposition": \{\par
      "title": "a. Biblical Explanation (What the Text Means)",\par
      "sections": \{\par
        "title": "Biblical Explanation",\par
        "points": [\par
          \{\par
            "scripture": "Jeremiah 1:5",\par
            "explanation": [\par
              "Purpose is pre-natal: God 'knew' and 'sanctified' the prophet before he was formed",\par
              "Our assignment is settled in heaven before it is manifested on earth"\par
            ]\par
          \},\par
          \{\par
            "scripture": "Ephesians 2:10",\par
            "explanation": [\par
              "We are God's 'workmanship' (poem/masterpiece), created for specific 'good works' prepared in advance",\par
              "Our job is to walk in the path God already paved"\par
            ]\par
          \},\par
          \{\par
            "scripture": "Proverbs 19:21",\par
            "explanation": [\par
              "Human plans are many, but only God's 'counsel' (purpose) will stand",\par
              "Success without purpose is eventually hollow"\par
            ]\par
          \}\par
        ]\par
      \}\par
    \},\par
    "theologicalClarification": \{\par
      "title": "b. Theological Clarification (Avoiding Extremes)",\par
      "points": [\par
        "Discovery vs. Invention: You do not 'create' your purpose; you 'discover' it through revelation.",\par
        "Progressive Revelation: God rarely shows the whole map at once; He reveals the next step of the path as we obey.",\par
        "Purpose vs. Career: A career is a *vehicle* (how you make a living), while purpose is the *destination* (why you live)."\par
      ]\par
    \},\par
    "doctrinalAlignment": \{\par
      "title": "c. Doctrinal Alignment",\par
      "points": [\par
        "The Sovereignty of God: God has a predetermined plan for history and individuals",\par
        "The Doctrine of Vocation: All work can be sacred if it aligns with God's calling",\par
        "Pneumatology: The Holy Spirit is the primary agent who reveals and empowers our calling"\par
      ]\par
    \},\par
    "keyTruths": [\par
      "Purpose precedes production\emdash God designed the 'Why' before the 'What'",\par
      "Your 'Holy Discontent' (what bothers you) often points to your calling",\par
      "Gifts and talents are indicators of your specific assignment",\par
      "Faithfulness in 'little' (the current season) unlocks the next stage of destiny",\par
      "Purpose is eternal; it impacts both this life and the one to come"\par
    ],\par
    "lifeApplication": [\par
      \{ "category": "Retreat", "instruction": "Spend one hour in total silence this week asking God: 'Lord, why did You make me?'" \},\par
      \{ "category": "Audit", "instruction": "List your 3 greatest passions and 3 greatest skills; look for where they intersect with a need in the world" \},\par
      \{ "category": "Journaling", "instruction": "Begin a 'Destiny Journal' to record recurring thoughts, burdens, or words from God" \},\par
      \{ "category": "Youth/Action", "instruction": "Choose one area of service in church that matches your natural inclinations and commit to it" \},\par
      \{ "category": "Mentorship", "instruction": "Identify an 'Elijah' (mentor) who is further ahead in your area of interest and ask for guidance" \}\par
    ],\par
    "discussionQuestions": [\par
      "What is the difference between a good idea and a 'God idea'?",\par
      "How does comparison with others kill our ability to walk in our unique purpose?",\par
      "Can a person be successful in their career but a failure in their divine purpose?"\par
    ],\par
    "caseStudy": \{\par
      "scenario": "A young adult is pressured by family to become a doctor for financial security, but they feel a deep burden and talent for youth reformation and creative arts.",\par
      "questions": [\par
        "How does Jeremiah 1:5 help this person navigate the pressure?",\par
        "What are the risks of choosing a career that contradicts one's divine design?"\par
      ]\par
    \},\par
    "personalReflection": [\par
      "Am I living to please people or to fulfill my assignment?",\par
      "What causes make my heart beat faster or move me to tears?",\par
      "If money were no object, what would I do for the Kingdom of God?"\par
    ],\par
    "actionPoint": "Write a 'Life Vision Statement' based on what you currently know about your gifts and God's leading."\par
  \},\par
  \par
  \{\par
    "id": 44,\par
    "title": "Lesson 44: Aligning Career with Divine Purpose",\par
    "texts": [\par
      "Exodus 31:1\endash 11",\par
      "Proverbs 22:29",\par
      "Colossians 3:23\endash 24",\par
      "Romans 12:4\endash 8"\par
    ],\par
    "lessonAim": \{\par
      "know": "Identify that every career is a potential platform for Kingdom expression",\par
      "believe": "Believe that God empowers professionals with skills and the Spirit to fulfill His purpose",\par
      "practice": "Choose career paths based on impact and calling rather than just status or income"\par
    \},\par
    "memoryVerse": \{\par
      "text": "In all thy ways acknowledge Him, and He shall direct thy paths.",\par
      "reference": "Proverbs 3:6 (KJV)"\par
    \},\par
    "introduction": [\par
      "Many believers face frustration because they separate career from divine purpose. In God's Kingdom, there is no secular-versus-sacred divide.",\par
      "Your work, business, and skills are platforms for fulfilling God's eternal purpose. Career is the vehicle; purpose is the destination."\par
    ],\par
    "introQuestion": "Are you working for a paycheck or for a purpose?",\par
    "exposition": \{\par
      "title": "a. Biblical Explanation (What the Text Means)",\par
      "sections": \{\par
        "title": "Biblical Explanation",\par
        "points": [\par
          \{\par
            "scripture": "Exodus 31:1\endash 11",\par
            "explanation": [\par
              "Divine Vocational Empowerment: God filled Bezalel with the Spirit specifically for craftsmanship and artisanship",\par
              "Professionalism as Calling: Building the Tabernacle required holy prophets *and* skilled professionals"\par
            ]\par
          \},\par
          \{\par
            "scripture": "Proverbs 22:29",\par
            "explanation": [\par
              "The Law of Excellence: Skillfulness in one's trade brings a person before 'kings' (influencers) rather than 'mean men'",\par
              "Competence is a prerequisite for Kingdom influence in the marketplace"\par
            ]\par
          \},\par
          \{\par
            "scripture": "Colossians 3:23\endash 24",\par
            "explanation": [\par
              "The True Employer: Believers work for the Lord Christ, not just human supervisors",\par
              "Excellence and integrity in secular work are actually acts of worship"\par
            ]\par
          \}\par
        ]\par
      \}\par
    \},\par
    "theologicalClarification": \{\par
      "title": "b. Theological Clarification (Avoiding Extremes)",\par
      "points": [\par
        "The Sacred/Secular Fallacy: Serving God is not limited to pulpit ministry; a godly accountant serves God's order as much as a preacher.",\par
        "Prosperity vs. Purpose: Financial success is a possible byproduct of career, but it is not the primary measure of alignment.",\par
        "Marketplace Ministry: You are a missionary 'sent' into your professional field to reflect Christ\rquote s light."\par
      ]\par
    \},\par
    "doctrinalAlignment": \{\par
      "title": "c. Doctrinal Alignment",\par
      "points": [\par
        "Common Grace: God gives skills and talents to all, but believers use them for His specific glory",\par
        "The Sovereignty of God: God places His people in strategic 'secular' positions (like Joseph or Daniel) to preserve His people",\par
        "Integrity: Kingdom values must supersede corporate greed or unethical shortcuts"\par
      ]\par
    \},\par
    "keyTruths": [\par
      "God calls professionals just as He calls prophets",\par
      "Your talent is a 'God-indicator' for your career direction",\par
      "Excellence is the currency of influence in the marketplace",\par
      "Work is a form of worship when done unto the Lord",\par
      "Career misalignment leads to burnout; alignment leads to fulfillment"\par
    ],\par
    "lifeApplication": [\par
      \{ "category": "Evaluation", "instruction": "Write down how your current job or studies can solve a problem for God's Kingdom" \},\par
      \{ "category": "Excellence", "instruction": "Identify one professional skill you need to master to become 'diligent' (Proverbs 22:29)" \},\par
      \{ "category": "Prayer", "instruction": "Pray specifically for your boss, colleagues, and the 'peace of the city' where you work" \},\par
      \{ "category": "Integrity", "instruction": "Resolve to speak truth and work honestly this week, even if it costs you a shortcut to profit" \},\par
      \{ "category": "Youth/Planning", "instruction": "Before choosing a major or trade, spend a day fasting to ask God: 'Where do You want to plant me?'" \}\par
    ],\par
    "discussionQuestions": [\par
      "How can a 'secular' career (like engineering or law) glorify God?",\par
      "What are the spiritual consequences of pursuing a career solely for money?",\par
      "How does being 'filled with the Spirit' affect a person's professional work?"\par
    ],\par
    "caseStudy": \{\par
      "scenario": "A gifted artist works in a bank because it pays well, but they feel depressed and disconnected from God's presence during the week.",\par
      "questions": [\par
        "Is this a 'provision' issue or a 'purpose' issue?",\par
        "How can they start transitioning their gift into their career path?"\par
      ]\par
    \},\par
    "personalReflection": [\par
      "If I were never paid for my job, would I still see its value in God's eyes?",\par
      "Am I a light in my workplace, or do I blend into the darkness?",\par
      "Is my career path a God-idea or just a good idea?"\par
    ],\par
    "actionPoint": "Draft a 'Marketplace Mission Statement'\emdash one sentence explaining how your career serves God's purpose."\par
  \},\par
  \par
  \par
  \par
  \{\par
    "id": 45,\par
    "title": "Lesson 45: Fulfilling Destiny through Divine Timing and Process",\par
    "texts": [\par
      "Ecclesiastes 3:1\endash 11",\par
      "Genesis 39\endash 41",\par
      "Hebrews 10:36",\par
      "Galatians 6:9"\par
    ],\par
    "lessonAim": \{\par
      "know": "Understand that destiny is a progressive journey requiring character development and divine timing",\par
      "believe": "Believe that waiting seasons are not wasted seasons, but periods of essential preparation",\par
      "practice": "Maintain faithfulness in obscurity and small assignments while waiting for the 'set time'"\par
    \},\par
    "memoryVerse": \{\par
      "text": "To every thing there is a season, and a time to every purpose under the heaven.",\par
      "reference": "Ecclesiastes 3:1 (KJV)"\par
    \},\par
    "introduction": [\par
      "Destiny is not microwaved; it is molded. Many abort their destiny because they grow impatient with God's process.",\par
      "Just as a seed must pass through seasons before bearing fruit, so must a person of purpose. Timing is as critical as the calling itself."\par
    ],\par
    "introQuestion": "Are you more focused on 'arriving' at your destiny or 'becoming' the person who can handle it?",\par
    "exposition": \{\par
      "title": "a. Biblical Explanation (What the Text Means)",\par
      "sections": \{\par
        "title": "Biblical Explanation",\par
        "points": [\par
          \{\par
            "scripture": "Ecclesiastes 3:1\endash 11",\par
            "explanation": [\par
              "Divine Chronology: God has a 'Kairos' (opportune time) for every 'Chronos' (linear time) event",\par
              "Beauty in Time: God makes all things beautiful only when they occur in His specific schedule"\par
            ]\par
          \},\par
          \{\par
            "scripture": "Genesis 39\endash 41 (The Joseph Cycle)",\par
            "explanation": [\par
              "The Pit, the Potiphar, and the Prison: These were not setbacks but the training ground for the Palace",\par
              "Character over Charisma: God tested Joseph's integrity in secret before promoting him in public"\par
            ]\par
          \},\par
          \{\par
            "scripture": "Hebrews 10:36",\par
            "explanation": [\par
              "The Endurance Link: Patience is the bridge between God's promise and the actual possession of the manifestation"\par
            ]\par
          \}\par
        ]\par
      \}\par
    \},\par
    "theologicalClarification": \{\par
      "title": "b. Theological Clarification (Avoiding Extremes)",\par
      "points": [\par
        "Preparation vs. Punishment: Hardship during the waiting season is often 'refining,' not 'rejection.'",\par
        "Sovereignty vs. Slothfulness: Waiting on God's timing does not mean doing nothing; it means being faithful with current small tasks.",\par
        "The Ishmael Trap: Rushing ahead of God's timing creates complications that the flesh cannot manage (Genesis 16)."\par
      ]\par
    \},\par
    "doctrinalAlignment": \{\par
      "title": "c. Doctrinal Alignment",\par
      "points": [\par
        "Sanctification: The process of destiny is the process of being made more like Christ",\par
        "Providence: God works all things (even betrayals) together for the ultimate 'expected end'",\par
        "Divine Stewardship: God entrusts destiny based on proven character"\par
      ]\par
    \},\par
    "keyTruths": [\par
      "God is more interested in the runner than the race",\par
      "Waiting is a period of active character building",\par
      "Premature exposure leads to a permanent collapse",\par
      "Faithfulness in the 'Prison' is the key to the 'Palace'",\par
      "Your current season is a prerequisite for your next season"\par
    ],\par
    "lifeApplication": [\par
      \{ "category": "Perspective", "instruction": "Identify your current season: Is it Pit (betrayal), Potiphar (service), or Prison (testing)?" \},\par
      \{ "category": "Faithfulness", "instruction": "Choose one 'small' task you've been neglecting and do it with total excellence this week" \},\par
      \{ "category": "Contentment", "instruction": "Stop comparing your 'Chapter 1' with someone else's 'Chapter 20'; trust your unique clock" \},\par
      \{ "category": "Journaling", "instruction": "Write down 3 lessons God has taught you during your current delay or waiting period" \},\par
      \{ "category": "Youth/Patience", "instruction": "Resist the urge to take 'shortcuts' to success that compromise your spiritual integrity" \}\par
    ],\par
    "discussionQuestions": [\par
      "Why does God allow a gap of time between the 'Dream' and the 'Destiny'?",\par
      "How can you tell the difference between a divine delay and a self-inflicted one?",\par
      "What character traits was God building in David while he was still tending sheep?"\par
    ],\par
    "caseStudy": \{\par
      "scenario": "A talented musician feels they should be leading the main choir, but they have been assigned to help the children's department for two years. They are becoming bitter.",\par
      "questions": [\par
        "Is this musician failing the 'faithfulness in little' test (Matthew 25:21)?",\par
        "What might God be trying to build in their heart before the 'big' stage?"\par
      ]\par
    \},\par
    "personalReflection": [\par
      "Am I trying to 'microwav'e a destiny that God wants to 'slow-cook'?",\par
      "Do I trust God's heart when I can't see His hand moving?",\par
      "Who am I becoming in the dark seasons of my life?"\par
    ],\par
    "actionPoint": "Declare every morning: 'My times are in Your hands. I will not rush; I will not lag; I will follow Your lead.'"\par
  \},\par
  \par
  \par
  \{\par
    "id": 46,\par
    "title": "Lesson 46: Destiny Fulfillment: Living a Life of Eternal Impact",\par
    "texts": [\par
      "2 Timothy 4:6\endash 8",\par
      "Matthew 25:14\endash 30",\par
      "John 17:4",\par
      "Acts 13:36"\par
    ],\par
    "lessonAim": \{\par
      "know": "Understand that destiny fulfillment is the completion of one's divine assignment with eternal value",\par
      "believe": "Believe that finishing strong requires sustained alignment, integrity, and daily surrender to God",\par
      "practice": "Evaluate current stewardship of gifts and commit to activities that produce lasting Kingdom fruit"\par
    \},\par
    "memoryVerse": \{\par
      "text": "I have fought a good fight, I have finished my course, I have kept the faith.",\par
      "reference": "2 Timothy 4:7 (KJV)"\par
    \},\par
    "introduction": [\par
      "Starting well is commendable, but finishing strong is essential. Destiny fulfillment is about completing your divine assignment with eternal rewards in view.",\par
      "A life of impact is sustained by character and a constant consciousness that we will one day stand before the judgment seat of Christ."\par
    ],\par
    "introQuestion": "If your life ended today, would you be able to say, like Jesus, 'It is finished'?",\par
    "exposition": \{\par
      "title": "a. Biblical Explanation (What the Text Means)",\par
      "sections": \{\par
        "title": "Biblical Explanation",\par
        "points": [\par
          \{\par
            "scripture": "2 Timothy 4:6\endash 8",\par
            "explanation": [\par
              "The Paul Model: Fulfillment is marked by a clear conscience, a completed task, and an unwavering faith",\par
              "The 'Crown of Righteousness' is the ultimate validation of a destiny-fulfilled life"\par
            ]\par
          \},\par
          \{\par
            "scripture": "John 17:4",\par
            "explanation": [\par
              "Glorifying God on earth is directly tied to 'finishing the work' He gave us to do",\par
              "Fulfillment is specific to the assignment, not just general busyness"\par
            ]\par
          \},\par
          \{\par
            "scripture": "1 Corinthians 3:12\endash 15",\par
            "explanation": [\par
              "The Fire Test: Works built with 'gold, silver, and precious stones' (eternal value) survive divine scrutiny",\par
              "Works built on 'wood, hay, and stubble' (earthly/selfish motives) will be burned up"\par
            ]\par
          \}\par
        ]\par
      \}\par
    \},\par
    "theologicalClarification": \{\par
      "title": "b. Theological Clarification (Avoiding Extremes)",\par
      "points": [\par
        "Fulfillment vs. Perfection: Fulfilling destiny doesn't mean you were perfect; it means you were faithful to your calling and repented when you strayed.",\par
        "Retirement vs. Refiring: In the Kingdom, there is no retirement from purpose. As long as there is breath, there is a dimension of the assignment to fulfill.",\par
        "Grace and Reward: We are saved by grace, but we are rewarded based on our works and faithfulness as stewards."\par
      ]\par
    \},\par
    "doctrinalAlignment": \{\par
      "title": "c. Doctrinal Alignment",\par
      "points": [\par
        "The Judgment Seat of Christ (Bema): The place where believers' works are evaluated for rewards",\par
        "The Doctrine of Perseverance: The necessity of the saints to endure in faith until the end",\par
        "Stewardship of Grace: Recognizing that our very ability to fulfill destiny comes from God's enabling power"\par
      ]\par
    \},\par
    "keyTruths": [\par
      "Destiny is about the finish line, not just the starting blocks",\par
      "A life of impact serves God\rquote s counsel in its own generation",\par
      "Character is the container that preserves your destiny",\par
      "Distraction is the greatest thief of eternal rewards",\par
      "Fulfillment is found in obedience, not just success"\par
    ],\par
    "lifeApplication": [\par
      \{ "category": "Legacy", "instruction": "Write out your 'Spiritual Eulogy'\emdash what you want God and men to say about your impact when you are gone" \},\par
      \{ "category": "Mentorship", "instruction": "Identify one person you can begin mentoring to ensure your impact outlives you" \},\par
      \{ "category": "Focus", "instruction": "Identify one 'good' activity that is currently distracting you from your 'God' assignment and prune it" \},\par
      \{ "category": "Accountability", "instruction": "Find a prayer partner to hold you accountable to your spiritual growth and character this month" \},\par
      \{ "category": "Youth/Habits", "instruction": "Audit your social media and screen time; redirect 30 minutes daily toward studying for your calling" \}\par
    ],\par
    "discussionQuestions": [\par
      "What is the difference between being 'successful' and being 'fruitful' in the Kingdom?",\par
      "How can secret sin disqualify a person from fulfilling their divine assignment?",\par
      "What does it mean to build with 'gold' in your daily career and family life?"\par
    ],\par
    "caseStudy": \{\par
      "scenario": "A man spent 40 years building a massive business empire but never shared the Gospel with his employees or raised his children in the Lord.",\par
      "questions": [\par
        "According to 1 Corinthians 3:12-15, what 'materials' was he building with?",\par
        "How does Acts 13:36 challenge this man's legacy?"\par
      ]\par
    \},\par
    "personalReflection": [\par
      "Am I building a monument to myself or a movement for the Kingdom?",\par
      "What is the one thing God told me to do that I have been putting off?",\par
      "Am I living every day with the awareness of the Judgment Seat?"\par
    ],\par
    "actionPoint": "Identify your 'major assignment' for this season and take one bold step toward completing it before the year ends."\par
  \},\par
  \par
