\f0 Discipleship Modules:\par
 \{ \par
    id: 1, \par
    title: "Lesson 1: Understanding Salvation", \par
    description: "Exploring the nature, problem, and pillars of God's rescue plan.",\par
    content: (\par
      <div className="space-y-2">\par
        <p className="font-bold">1. What is Salvation?</p>\par
        <p>Salvation is God\f1\rquote\f0 s complete work of delivering humanity from the penalty, power, and ultimately the presence of sin, and restoring us into right relationship with Himself through Jesus Christ.</p>\par
        <p>Salvation is not:</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>Church attendance</li>\par
          <li>Moral reform</li>\par
          <li>Emotional experience</li>\par
          <li>Family inheritance</li>\par
        </ul>\par
        <p>Salvation is:</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>A divine rescue (Colossians 1:13\f1\endash 14)</li>\par
          <li>A spiritual rebirth (John 3:3)</li>\par
          <li>A legal declaration of righteousness (Romans 5:1)</li>\par
          <li>A relational restoration (2 Corinthians 5:18\endash 19)</li>\par
        </ul>\par
        <p>Biblically, salvation has three dimensions:</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>Justification \endash  We are saved from sin\rquote s penalty.</li>\par
          <li>Sanctification \endash  We are being saved from sin\rquote s power.</li>\par
          <li>Glorification \endash  We will be saved from sin\rquote s presence.</li>\par
        </ul>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">2. The Problem of Sin</p>\par
        <p>Key Text: Romans 3:23</p>\par
        <p>\ldblquote For all have sinned and fall short of the glory of God.\rdblquote </p>\par
        <p>What is Sin?</p>\par
        <p>Sin is:</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>Missing God\rquote s standard (Romans 3:23)</li>\par
          <li>Rebellion against God (Isaiah 53:6)</li>\par
          <li>Lawlessness (1 John 3:4)</li>\par
        </ul>\par
        <p>The Effects of Sin</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>Spiritual death (Romans 6:23)</li>\par
          <li>Separation from God (Isaiah 59:2)</li>\par
          <li>Corrupted human nature (Jeremiah 17:9)</li>\par
          <li>Universal guilt (Romans 5:12)</li>\par
        </ul>\par
        <p>Sin is not merely behavior \emdash  it is a condition.</p>\par
        <p>We are not sinners because we sin; we sin because we are sinners.</p>\par
        <p>Cultural Application</p>\par
        <p>In many contexts, sin is minimized to:</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>\ldblquote Mistake\rdblquote </li>\par
          <li>\ldblquote Human weakness\rdblquote </li>\par
          <li>\ldblquote Village curse\rdblquote </li>\par
          <li>\ldblquote Spiritual attack\rdblquote </li>\par
        </ul>\par
        <p>But Scripture teaches personal responsibility (Ezekiel 18:20).</p>\par
        <p>Salvation begins when we acknowledge guilt before God.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">3. Justification, Regeneration, and Adoption</p>\par
        <p>These are three core theological pillars of salvation.</p>\par
        <p className="font-semibold">A. Justification</p>\par
        <p>Definition: A legal act where God declares the sinner righteous based on Christ\rquote s finished work.</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>Romans 5:1</li>\par
          <li>2 Corinthians 5:21</li>\par
          <li>Galatians 2:16</li>\par
        </ul>\par
        <p>Justification does not mean we become morally perfect instantly.</p>\par
        <p>It means our legal standing before God changes.</p>\par
        <p>It is: Instant, Complete, Based on Christ alone.</p>\par
        \par
        <p className="font-semibold pt-1">B. Regeneration</p>\par
        <p>Definition: The spiritual rebirth produced by the Holy Spirit.</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>John 3:5\endash 8</li>\par
          <li>Titus 3:5</li>\par
          <li>2 Corinthians 5:17</li>\par
        </ul>\par
        <p>Regeneration changes: Our nature, Our desires, Our spiritual capacity.</p>\par
        <p>Before regeneration \f3\u8594?\f1  \f0 spiritually dead (Ephesians 2:1)</p>\par
        <p>After regeneration \f3\u8594?\f1  \f0 spiritually alive (Ephesians 2:5)</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-semibold pt-1">C. Adoption</p>\par
        <p>Definition: God brings us into His family as sons and daughters.</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>Romans 8:15\f1\endash 17</li>\par
          <li>Galatians 4:4\endash 7</li>\par
          <li>John 1:12</li>\par
        </ul>\par
        <p>Adoption gives us: Access, Inheritance, Intimacy, Identity.</p>\par
        <p>We are not merely forgiven criminals. We are adopted children.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">4. Grace vs Works</p>\par
        <p>Salvation is by Grace</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>Ephesians 2:8\endash 9</li>\par
          <li>Romans 11:6</li>\par
          <li>Titus 3:5</li>\par
        </ul>\par
        <p>Grace means: Undeserved favor, Unmerited kindness, Divine initiative.</p>\par
        <p>We do not work for salvation. We work because of salvation (Ephesians 2:10).</p>\par
        <p>The Danger of Legalism: Legalism says: \ldblquote If I perform well, God will accept me.\rdblquote  The gospel says: \ldblquote God has accepted me in Christ, therefore I obey.\rdblquote </p>\par
        <p>The Danger of Cheap Grace: Grace does not mean: License to sin (Romans 6:1\endash 2), Casual Christianity. True grace transforms.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">5. Assurance of Salvation</p>\par
        <p>Many believers struggle with assurance because they base it on feelings.</p>\par
        <p>Assurance is grounded in:</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>The Promise of God (John 5:24)</li>\par
          <li>The Finished Work of Christ (Hebrews 10:14)</li>\par
          <li>The Witness of the Spirit (Romans 8:16)</li>\par
          <li>The Evidence of Transformation (1 John 2:3)</li>\par
        </ul>\par
        <p>Salvation is secured by Christ, not by emotional stability.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">6. Evidence of Genuine Conversion</p>\par
        <p>True salvation produces visible fruit.</p>\par
        <p>A. New Desires: Love for God (1 John 4:19), Hunger for the Word (1 Peter 2:2)</p>\par
        <p>B. Obedience: 1 John 2:3\endash 6</p>\par
        <p>C. Love for Others: 1 John 3:14</p>\par
        <p>D. Progressive Growth: Philippians 1:6. Not perfection \emdash  but direction. Not sinless \emdash  but no longer comfortable in sin.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">BIBLICAL CASE STUDY</p>\par
        <p>Zacchaeus (Luke 19:1\endash 10)</p>\par
        <p>Evidence of real conversion:</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>Conviction</li>\par
          <li>Public identification with Christ</li>\par
          <li>Restitution</li>\par
          <li>Changed behavior</li>\par
        </ul>\par
        <p>Jesus said: \ldblquote Today salvation has come to this house.\rdblquote  Salvation always produces transformation.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">DISCUSSION QUESTIONS</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>Why is understanding sin essential before understanding salvation?</li>\par
          <li>What is the difference between justification and regeneration?</li>\par
          <li>Why can good works never save?</li>\par
          <li>How can a believer be sure of salvation?</li>\par
          <li>What are practical signs of genuine conversion?</li>\par
        </ul>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">PERSONAL REFLECTION</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>Have I truly repented or merely become religious?</li>\par
          <li>What evidences of transformation can I identify in my life?</li>\par
          <li>Am I trusting Christ or my performance?</li>\par
        </ul>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">ACTION STEPS (WEEKLY ASSIGNMENT)</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>Memorize Ephesians 2:8\endash 9.</li>\par
          <li>Write your salvation testimony (before Christ, how you met Him, after Christ).</li>\par
          <li>Identify one area where transformation must become visible.</li>\par
          <li>Begin daily Bible reading (Start with the Gospel of John).</li>\par
        </ul>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">MEMORY VERSE</p>\par
        <p>2 Corinthians 5:17 \emdash  \ldblquote Therefore, if anyone is in Christ, he is a new creation; old things have passed away; behold, all things have become new.\rdblquote </p>\par
      </div>\par
    )\par
  \},\par
