\{ \par
    id: 2, \par
    title: "Lesson 2: What is a Disciple?", \par
    description: "Moving from being a church member to an intentional follower of Christ.",\par
    content: (\par
      <div className="space-y-2">\par
        <p className="font-bold">INTRODUCTION</p>\par
        <p>Salvation brings us into God\rquote s family.<br />\par
        Discipleship forms us into Christ\rquote s likeness.<br />\par
        Many are saved.<br />\par
        Few are discipled.<br />\par
        Many attend church.<br />\par
        Few follow Christ intentionally.<br />\par
        Christianity is not merely about conversion \emdash  it is about transformation.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">1. What is a Disciple?</p>\par
        <p className="font-semibold">Definition</p>\par
        <p>Key Text: Matthew 28:19\endash 20<br />\par
        \ldblquote\f0 Go therefore and make disciples of all nations\f1\'85 \f0 teaching them to observe all things that I have commanded you\f1\'85\rdblquote </p>\par
        <p>The command of Jesus was not:</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>\ldblquote Make converts\rdblquote </li>\par
          <li>\ldblquote Make church members\rdblquote </li>\par
          <li>\ldblquote Make emotional responders\rdblquote </li>\par
        </ul>\par
        <p>The command was: Make disciples.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-semibold pt-1">The Word \ldblquote Disciple\rdblquote </p>\par
        <p>The Greek word <em>mathetes</em> means:</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>Learner</li>\par
          <li>Student</li>\par
          <li>Apprentice</li>\par
          <li>One who follows to become like the teacher</li>\par
        </ul>\par
        <p>A disciple is not merely someone who believes in Jesus.<br />\par
        A disciple is someone who follows Jesus to become like Jesus.</p>\par
        <p><strong>A working definition:</strong><br />\par
        A disciple is a saved person who is intentionally learning from Christ, obeying His Word, and helping others follow Him.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">2. Disciple vs Church Member</p>\par
        <p>Luke 6:40<br />\par
        \ldblquote A disciple is not above his teacher, but everyone who is perfectly trained will be like his teacher.\rdblquote </p>\par
        <p><strong>Church Member:</strong> Identifies with a congregation, May attend services, May give offerings, May participate occasionally.</p>\par
        <p><strong>Disciple:</strong> Follows Christ daily, Submits to His authority, Imitates His character, Lives under biblical instruction, Reproduces spiritually.</p>\par
        <p>A church member may attend without transformation.<br />\par
        A disciple cannot follow without transformation.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-semibold pt-1">Practical Difference</p>\par
        <table className="min-w-full border-collapse border border-gray-300 my-2">\par
          <thead>\par
            <tr>\par
              <th className="border border-gray-300 p-2">Church Member</th>\par
              <th className="border border-gray-300 p-2">Disciple</th>\par
            </tr>\par
          </thead>\par
          <tbody>\par
            <tr>\par
              <td className="border border-gray-300 p-2">Goes to church</td>\par
              <td className="border border-gray-300 p-2">Walks with Christ</td>\par
            </tr>\par
            <tr>\par
              <td className="border border-gray-300 p-2">Listens to sermons</td>\par
              <td className="border border-gray-300 p-2">Applies truth</td>\par
            </tr>\par
            <tr>\par
              <td className="border border-gray-300 p-2">Knows Christian language</td>\par
              <td className="border border-gray-300 p-2">Lives Christian lifestyle</td>\par
            </tr>\par
            <tr>\par
              <td className="border border-gray-300 p-2">May depend on pastor</td>\par
              <td className="border border-gray-300 p-2">Studies personally</td>\par
            </tr>\par
            <tr>\par
              <td className="border border-gray-300 p-2">Adds to attendance</td>\par
              <td className="border border-gray-300 p-2">Multiplies believers</td>\par
            </tr>\par
          </tbody>\par
        </table>\par
        <p>The early believers were first called Christians in Antioch (Acts 11:26) \emdash  but before they were called Christians, they were disciples.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">3. The Cost of Discipleship</p>\par
        <p>Luke 9:23\endash 25<br />\par
        \ldblquote If anyone desires to come after Me, let him deny himself, and take up his cross daily, and follow Me.\rdblquote </p>\par
        <p>Jesus never hid the cost.</p>\par
        <p><strong>A. Self-Denial:</strong> Denying self means: Surrendering personal will, Rejecting self-centered living, Choosing obedience over comfort.</p>\par
        <p><strong>B. Taking Up the Cross Daily:</strong> The cross represents: Death to self, Public identification with Christ, Willingness to suffer for righteousness. It is daily \emdash  not occasional.</p>\par
        <p><strong>C. Following Him:</strong> Following implies: Movement, Direction, Progress.</p>\par
        <p><strong>The Great Exchange (Luke 9:24\endash 25):</strong> Save your life \f3\u8594?\f1  \f0 lose it. Lose your life for Christ \f3\u8594?\f1  \f0 save it.<br />\par
        Discipleship costs comfort, ego, and independence. But it produces eternal life and eternal reward.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">4. Abiding in Christ</p>\par
        <p>John 15:1\f1\endash 8<br />\par
        Jesus describes Himself as: The Vine, We are the branches.</p>\par
        <p>Abiding means: Remaining connected, Staying dependent, Continual fellowship.<br />\par
        A branch cannot produce fruit by effort. It produces by connection.</p>\par
        <p><strong>Results of Abiding:</strong> Fruitfulness (John 15:5), Spiritual vitality, Answered prayer (John 15:7), Glorifying the Father (John 15:8).<br />\par
        Discipleship is not behavior modification. It is life flowing from union with Christ.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">5. Biblical Models of Discipleship</p>\par
        <p><strong>A. Antioch Church \endash  Acts 11:26:</strong> Believers were taught consistently. Discipleship involved: Instruction, Community, Identity. They were disciples before they were labeled Christians.</p>\par
        <p><strong>B. Multiplication Model \endash  2 Timothy 2:2:</strong> \ldblquote\f0 The things you have heard from me\f1\'85 \f0 commit these to faithful men who will be able to teach others also.\f1\rdblquote <br />\par
        Four generations: Paul \f3\u8594?\f1  \f0 Timothy \f3\u8594?\f1  \f0 Faithful men \f3\u8594?\f1  \f0 Others.<br />\par
        True discipleship reproduces itself. If discipleship does not multiply, it is incomplete.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">6. PRACTICAL APPLICATION</p>\par
        <p className="font-semibold">A. Personal Discipleship Covenant</p>\par
        <p>Every disciple should consciously commit.<br />\par
        Sample Personal Covenant: \f1\ldblquote\f0 I commit to: Daily prayer and Bible study. Obeying God\f1\rquote\f0 s Word. Participating actively in church life. Living a holy and accountable life. Sharing my faith regularly. Submitting to spiritual guidance. Growing to disciple others.\f1\rdblquote\f0 <br />\par
        Discipleship without commitment becomes convenience.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-semibold pt-1">B. Accountability Structure</p>\par
        <p>Discipleship thrives in structure.</p>\par
        <p><strong>1. One-on-One Mentorship:</strong> Weekly or biweekly meeting, Scripture discussion, Life accountability, Prayer.</p>\par
        <p><strong>2. Small Discipleship Groups:</strong> 3\f1\endash 5 members, Bible study, Confession and encouragement (James 5:16), Practical growth tracking.</p>\par
        <p><strong>3. Growth Metrics:</strong> A disciple should be growing in: Character (Galatians 5:22\endash 23), Knowledge (2 Peter 3:18), Service (1 Peter 4:10), Evangelism (Matthew 4:19), Consistency.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">SIGNS OF A TRUE DISCIPLE</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>Teachable spirit</li>\par
          <li>Hunger for Scripture</li>\par
          <li>Obedience</li>\par
          <li>Spiritual discipline</li>\par
          <li>Kingdom-mindedness</li>\par
          <li>Reproductive mindset</li>\par
        </ul>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">CULTURAL DISCUSSION</p>\par
        <p>In many contexts: Christianity is inherited. Church attendance replaces spiritual growth. Titles replace transformation.<br />\par
        But Jesus did not call us to carry titles. He called us to carry crosses.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">DISCUSSION QUESTIONS</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>What distinguishes a disciple from a regular church attendee?</li>\par
          <li>Why did Jesus emphasize the cost of following Him?</li>\par
          <li>What does abiding practically look like in daily life?</li>\par
          <li>Who is discipling you?</li>\par
          <li>Who are you discipling?</li>\par
        </ul>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">PERSONAL REFLECTION</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>Am I truly following Christ or merely attending church?</li>\par
          <li>What areas of self still resist surrender?</li>\par
          <li>Is my life producing spiritual fruit?</li>\par
        </ul>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">WEEKLY ASSIGNMENT</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>Memorize Luke 9:23.</li>\par
          <li>Write your discipleship commitment covenant.</li>\par
          <li>Identify one mature believer for accountability.</li>\par
          <li>Identify one younger believer to mentor.</li>\par
        </ul>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">MEMORY VERSE</p>\par
        <p>Matthew 28:19 \emdash  \ldblquote\f0 Go therefore and make disciples of all nations\f1\'85\rdblquote </p>\par
      </div>\par
    )\par
  \},\par
\par
