\{ \par
    id: 6, \par
    title: "Lesson 6: The Word of God", \par
    description: "Discovering the authority, necessity, and practical methods for studying the Bible.",\par
    content: (\par
      <div className="space-y-2">\par
        <p className="font-bold">INTRODUCTION</p>\par
        <p>Spiritual growth is impossible without Scripture.<br />\par
        Prayer connects us to God relationally.<br />\par
        The Word anchors us doctrinally.</p>\par
        <p>A believer who neglects the Word becomes: Spiritually unstable, Doctrinally confused, Emotionally driven, Easily deceived.</p>\par
        <p>The Word of God is not optional equipment \emdash  it is spiritual oxygen.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">1. Inspiration and Authority of Scripture</p>\par
        <p>2 Timothy 3:16\endash 17 \emdash  \ldblquote\f0 All Scripture is given by inspiration of God, and is profitable for doctrine, for reproof, for correction, for instruction in righteousness\f1\'85\rdblquote </p>\par
        <p><strong>A. Inspiration of Scripture:</strong> \ldblquote Inspiration\rdblquote  (Greek: <em>theopneustos</em>) means: God-breathed. Scripture is: Not human opinion, Not cultural invention, Not merely historical literature. It is divinely inspired revelation. God used human authors, but preserved divine authority.</p>\par
        <p><strong>B. Authority of Scripture:</strong> Because it is God-breathed, it is: Final authority in doctrine, Final authority in morality, Final authority in spiritual direction. Not: Culture, Tradition, Emotions, Popular opinion. If Scripture is inspired, it must also be obeyed.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">2. Why the Word is Essential for Spiritual Formation</p>\par
        <p>According to 2 Timothy 3:16\endash 17, Scripture:</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>Teaches what is right (Doctrine)</li>\par
          <li>Corrects what is wrong (Reproof)</li>\par
          <li>Restores what is broken (Correction)</li>\par
          <li>Trains in righteousness (Instruction)</li>\par
        </ul>\par
        <p>Result: \ldblquote\'85\f0 that the man of God may be complete\f1\'85\rdblquote  Spiritual maturity is Word-formed.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">3. Meditation on the Word</p>\par
        <p>Joshua 1:8 \emdash  \ldblquote\f0 This Book of the Law shall not depart from your mouth, but you shall meditate in it day and night\f1\'85\rdblquote </p>\par
        <p>Meditation is not emptying the mind. It is filling the mind repeatedly with truth. Biblical meditation involves: Reading, Reflecting, Repeating, Personalizing, Praying Scripture. Meditation moves truth: From information \f3\u8594?\f1  \f0 to transformation.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">4. Rightly Dividing the Word</p>\par
        <p>2 Timothy 2:15 \f1\emdash  \ldblquote\f0 Be diligent\f1\'85 \f0 rightly dividing the word of truth.\f1\rdblquote  This means: Interpreting correctly, Respecting context, Avoiding distortion, Handling Scripture responsibly.</p>\par
        <p>Common errors to avoid: Taking verses out of context, Reading personal meaning into the text, Ignoring historical and literary background, Building doctrine from isolated verses. Sound disciples study carefully \emdash  not casually.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">5. Applying Scripture Practically</p>\par
        <p>James 1:22\endash 25 \emdash  \ldblquote\f0 Be doers of the word, and not hearers only\f1\'85\rdblquote  Application is the goal of Bible study. Without application: Knowledge becomes pride, Revelation becomes stagnation, Hearing becomes deception.</p>\par
        <p>Every study should answer:</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>What does this teach about God?</li>\par
          <li>What does this reveal about humanity?</li>\par
          <li>Is there a command to obey?</li>\par
          <li>Is there a promise to trust?</li>\par
          <li>Is there a sin to avoid?</li>\par
        </ul>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">PRACTICAL TOOLS FOR BIBLE STUDY</p>\par
        <p className="font-semibold">1. The Inductive Bible Study Method</p>\par
        <p>Inductive study follows three steps:</p>\par
        <p><strong>A. Observation \endash  What does it say?</strong> Who is speaking? Who is the audience? What is happening? Repeated words? Key themes? Do not interpret before observing.</p>\par
        <p><strong>B. Interpretation \endash  What does it mean?</strong> What was the author\rquote s original intent? What does the context reveal? How does it fit the whole Bible? Scripture interprets Scripture.</p>\par
        <p><strong>C. Application \endash  How does this apply to me?</strong> What must I change? What must I start? What must I stop? Truth is incomplete until obeyed.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-semibold pt-1">2. The SOAP Method</p>\par
        <p>A simple devotional approach: <strong>S</strong> \endash  Scripture (Write the verse), <strong>O</strong> \endash  Observation (What stands out?), <strong>A</strong> \endash  Application (How does this apply personally?), <strong>P</strong> \endash  Prayer (Pray the truth back to God).</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-semibold pt-1">3. Scripture Journaling Template</p>\par
        <p>Date, Passage, Key Verse, Main Theme, What it teaches about God, What it reveals about me, Command to obey, Promise to claim, Personal application, Prayer response. Journaling strengthens retention and reflection.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">6. Memorization of Scripture</p>\par
        <p>Psalm 119:11 \emdash  \ldblquote\f0 Your word I have hidden in my heart\f1\'85\rdblquote  Memorization internalizes truth. Benefits: Strength against temptation, Renewed thinking, Immediate spiritual response, Confidence in prayer. Practical method: Choose one verse weekly, Write it down, Repeat daily, Recite aloud, Apply intentionally.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">CULTURAL REFLECTION</p>\par
        <p>In many settings: Prophetic words replace Scripture study. Sermons replace personal devotion. Emotional experiences replace doctrinal grounding. But spiritual maturity requires: Personal engagement with the Word. The Spirit will never contradict Scripture. A church may be noisy without depth if Scripture is neglected.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">PRACTICAL DISCIPLINE PLAN (Next 30 Days)</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>Read one Gospel chapter daily.</li>\par
          <li>Journal using SOAP or Inductive method.</li>\par
          <li>Memorize one verse per week.</li>\par
          <li>Meet weekly with accountability partner to discuss insights.</li>\par
        </ul>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">DISCUSSION QUESTIONS</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>Why is Scripture final authority?</li>\par
          <li>What is the difference between reading and meditating?</li>\par
          <li>Why is application critical?</li>\par
          <li>How can wrong interpretation damage spiritual growth?</li>\par
          <li>Which method works best for you \emdash  Inductive or SOAP?</li>\par
        </ul>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">PERSONAL REFLECTION</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>Is the Word shaping my thinking?</li>\par
          <li>Do I study or merely skim?</li>\par
          <li>When last did Scripture confront and change me?</li>\par
        </ul>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">WEEKLY ASSIGNMENT</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>Memorize 2 Timothy 3:16\endash 17.</li>\par
          <li>Practice the Inductive method on one chapter this week.</li>\par
          <li>Start a Scripture journal.</li>\par
          <li>Share one insight with your accountability partner.</li>\par
        </ul>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">MEMORY VERSE</p>\par
        <p>Joshua 1:8 \emdash  \ldblquote\f0 This Book of the Law shall not depart from your mouth, but you shall meditate in it day and night\f1\'85\rdblquote </p>\par
      </div>\par
    )\par
  \},\par
\par
\par
\par
