\{ \par
    id: 9, \par
    title: "Lesson 9: Character & Inner Transformation", \par
    description: "Moving beyond behavior modification to true Christ-likeness and heart transformation.",\par
    content: (\par
      <div className="space-y-2">\par
        <p className="font-bold">INTRODUCTION</p>\par
        <p>Discipleship is not behavior modification; it is inner transformation. Christianity is not merely believing the right doctrines\emdash it is becoming the right kind of person.</p>\par
        <p>Real disciples are recognized by <strong>character</strong>, not by the volume of prayer, spiritual gifts, or public ministry. God is more committed to forming Christ in you than promoting you. (Galatians 4:19)</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-4 text-lg">PART I: THE CHARACTER OF CHRIST</p>\par
        <p>The goal is Christ-likeness (Romans 8:29). Let's examine core qualities of His character:</p>\par
        \par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">1. HUMILITY</p>\par
        <p>Humility is accurate self-assessment under God\rquote s authority. It is not weakness or self-hatred; it is recognizing your dependence on God and serving without needing recognition (Philippians 2:5\endash 8).</p>\par
        <p><strong>True Humility:</strong> Accepts correction, serves quietly, and celebrates others. It attracts grace (James 4:6).</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">2. OBEDIENCE</p>\par
        <p>Obedience is the alignment of your will with God\rquote s revealed will (John 6:38). It is love expressed practically (John 14:15). Remember: <em>Delayed obedience is disobedience.</em></p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">3. INTEGRITY</p>\par
        <p>Integrity is the consistency between your public life, private life, and inner thoughts. It means "wholeness." If character collapses in private, destiny eventually collapses in public (Psalms 15).</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">4. COMPASSION</p>\par
        <p>Compassion is love that moves toward suffering (Matthew 9:36). It is not just feeling bad; it is taking action. True Christ-like character combines <strong>Truth + Mercy</strong>.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-4 text-lg">PART II: THE BEATITUDES \emdash  THE DNA OF KINGDOM CHARACTER</p>\par
        <p>Found in Matthew 5, these describe the essential traits of a kingdom citizen:</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li><strong>Poverty of Spirit:</strong> Acknowledging "I need God." It is the opposite of self-sufficiency.</li>\par
          <li><strong>Meekness:</strong> Strength under control. Meek people don't retaliate or need to win every argument; they trust God for vindication.</li>\par
          <li><strong>Hunger for Righteousness:</strong> Spiritual appetite. You crave what you value.</li>\par
          <li><strong>Mercy:</strong> Withholding deserved judgment. It reflects God\rquote s heart toward us.</li>\par
          <li><strong>Purity of Heart:</strong> Internal cleanliness and sincere motives. Purity produces spiritual clarity\emdash you will "see God."</li>\par
        </ul>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">WHY THIS IS CRUCIAL</p>\par
        <p>Gifts may attract people, but <strong>character sustains impact</strong>. Charisma builds crowds, but integrity builds legacy. Spiritual maturity is proven by how you treat the weak and how you behave when unseen.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">PRACTICAL TRANSFORMATION PROCESS</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>Daily Scripture meditation.</li>\par
          <li>Honest weekly self-examination.</li>\par
          <li>Immediate repentance when convicted.</li>\par
          <li>Regular accountability relationships.</li>\par
        </ul>\par
        <p>Transformation is progressive\emdash from "glory to glory" (2 Corinthians 3:18).</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">SELF-EVALUATION QUESTIONS</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>Do I defend myself more than I examine myself?</li>\par
          <li>Am I teachable?</li>\par
          <li>Is my private life aligned with my public image?</li>\par
          <li>Am I compassionate toward weakness?</li>\par
        </ul>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">WEEKLY ASSIGNMENT</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>Practice "unseen service"\emdash do something helpful that no one else will find out about.</li>\par
          <li>Memorize 2 Corinthians 3:18.</li>\par
          <li>Identify one area of your private life that needs to align with your public confession.</li>\par
        </ul>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">CONCLUSION</p>\par
        <p>Character is slow to build\emdash but it is the only thing that lasts. God is building sons and daughters, not celebrities.</p>\par
      </div>\par
    )\par
  \},\par
\par
