\{ \par
    id: 18, \par
    title: "Lesson 18: Financial Discipleship & Stewardship", \par
    description: "Aligning wealth with worship, breaking the spirit of greed, and mastering practical money management.",\par
    content: (\par
      <div className="space-y-2">\par
        <p className="font-bold">INTRODUCTION</p>\par
        <p>Money is not merely economic\emdash it is spiritual. Jesus spoke extensively about finances because they reveal the condition of the heart: <em>\ldblquote For where your treasure is, there your heart will be also\rdblquote </em> (Matthew 6:21). Financial discipleship is about moving from being a "consumer" to a "steward."</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-4 text-lg">PART I: BIBLICAL THEOLOGY OF MONEY</p>\par
        \par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">1. The Nature of Money</p>\par
        <p>Money itself is a neutral tool; it is the <strong>love of money</strong> that is the root of evil (1 Timothy 6:10). Money simply magnifies what is already in your heart\emdash it can multiply either generosity or selfishness.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">2. Prosperity vs. Greed</p>\par
        <p>Biblical prosperity is connected to soul health (3 John 1:2) and fruitfulness. Greed, however, is never satisfied and is driven by comparison and fear. In the Kingdom, <strong>prosperity makes money a servant; greed makes it a master.</strong></p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">3. Kingdom Economics</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li><strong>Ownership:</strong> Everything belongs to God (Psalm 24:1); we are simply managers.</li>\par
          <li><strong>Giving:</strong> Generosity breaks the power of greed and demonstrates trust (Luke 6:38).</li>\par
          <li><strong>Increase:</strong> Faithfulness with small amounts leads to greater responsibility (Matthew 25:14\endash 30).</li>\par
        </ul>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-4 text-lg">PART II: PERSONAL FINANCIAL MANAGEMENT</p>\par
        \par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">1. Budgeting (Proverbs 21:5)</p>\par
        <p>A budget is a plan that aligns your spending with your values. Untracked money is unmanaged money. <strong>Principle:</strong> Live below your means and include a margin for emergencies.</p>\par
        \par
        \par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">2. Saving & Investing</p>\par
        <p>Wisdom stores up for the future (Proverbs 6:6\endash 8). \par
          <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
            <li><strong>Emergency Fund:</strong> Aim for 3\endash 6 months of expenses to protect against job loss or repairs.</li>\par
            <li><strong>Investing:</strong> Build long-term stability through diversification and patience. Avoid "get-rich-quick" schemes.</li>\par
          </ul>\par
        </p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">3. Avoiding the Debt Trap</p>\par
        <p>Debt enslaves the borrower to the lender (Proverbs 22:7). Aggressively pay off high-interest debt and refuse to finance a lifestyle you cannot afford. Debt reduces your spiritual and financial flexibility.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-4 text-lg">PART III: FUTURE STEWARDSHIP</p>\par
        <p>Stewardship includes protecting your family through <strong>Insurance</strong> (health, life, property) and <strong>Estate Planning</strong> (wills and guardianships). This ensures that your resources continue to bless your lineage without confusion.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">PRACTICAL IMPLEMENTATION PLAN</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5 text-sm">\par
          <li><strong>Give First:</strong> Automate your tithe or first-fruits giving.</li>\par
          <li><strong>Save Consistently:</strong> Set up a recurring transfer to an emergency fund.</li>\par
          <li><strong>Spend Intentionally:</strong> Before a major purchase, ask: <em>"Is this a need or an impulse?"</em></li>\par
        </ul>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">DISCUSSION QUESTIONS</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>Does money\emdash or the lack of it\emdash currently control my peace of mind?</li>\par
          <li>Do I have a written plan for my income, or am I "winging it" monthly?</li>\par
          <li>How can I teach the next generation the joy of giving and the value of work?</li>\par
        </ul>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">WEEKLY ASSIGNMENT</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>Track every single penny you spend for the next 7 days.</li>\par
          <li>Identify one recurring "lifestyle" expense you can cut to increase your giving or saving.</li>\par
          <li>Memorize Matthew 6:21.</li>\par
        </ul>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">CONCLUSION</p>\par
        <p>Wealth is not the goal; faithfulness is. When money is surrendered to God, anxiety decreases and freedom expands. Let your finances preach your faith.</p>\par
      </div>\par
    )\par
  \},\par
\par
\par
\par
