\{ \par
    id: 19, \par
    title: "Lesson 19: Giving & Generosity", \par
    description: "A balanced exploration of tithing, New Testament generosity, and missions support without legalism.",\par
    content: (\par
      <div className="space-y-2">\par
        <p className="font-bold">INTRODUCTION</p>\par
        <p>Few topics generate as much debate as money. To handle this faithfully, we must distinguish between covenant contexts and avoid extremes. Giving is not fundraising; it is worship. As Jesus said, <em>\ldblquote It is more blessed to give than to receive\rdblquote </em> (Acts 20:35).</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-4 text-lg">PART I: TITHING \emdash  THEOLOGY & DEBATES</p>\par
        <p>\ldblquote Tithe\rdblquote  means a tenth. While it was practiced by Abraham before the Law (Genesis 14:20), it functioned as a religious tax under the Mosaic Covenant to support the Levites and the Temple.</p>\par
        \par
        <p className="font-semibold pt-2">The New Testament Perspective</p>\par
        <p>The New Testament does not explicitly command a fixed 10% for the Church. Instead, it emphasizes Spirit-led, proportional, and joyful giving: <em>\ldblquote\f0 Each one must give as he has decided in his heart\f1\'85 \f0 not reluctantly or under compulsion\f1\rdblquote </em> (2 Corinthians 9:7). For many, 10% is a <strong>helpful starting point</strong>, but grace calls us to grow beyond percentages into sacrificial love.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-4 text-lg">PART II: OFFERINGS & SACRIFICIAL GIVING</p>\par
        <p>An offering is giving beyond the regular amount. God measures sacrifice, not just the size of the gift. Jesus praised the widow who gave two small coins (Mark 12:41\endash 44) because she gave out of her poverty. <strong>Giving is a worshipful response, not a transaction to control God.</strong></p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-4 text-lg">PART III: SUPPORTING MISSIONS</p>\par
        <p>The Great Commission (Matthew 28:19\endash 20) requires funding for travel, resources, and worker support. Paul frequently thanked churches for their financial partnership (Philippians 4:15\endash 17). Giving to missions is a direct investment in the eternal harvest of souls.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-4 text-lg">PART IV: DEVELOPING A GENEROUS LIFESTYLE</p>\par
        <p>Generosity reveals where your allegiance lies (Matthew 6:21). It breaks the power of money as an idol and declares God as your source.</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5 text-sm">\par
          <li><strong>Start Structured:</strong> Choose a consistent percentage to begin.</li>\par
          <li><strong>Increase Gradually:</strong> As income grows, increase your generosity.</li>\par
          <li><strong>Give Anonymously:</strong> Protect your humility and focus on God.</li>\par
          <li><strong>Budget for Giving:</strong> Plan to give first; don't wait for leftovers.</li>\par
        </ul>\par
\par
        \par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">COMMON ERRORS TO AVOID</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5 text-sm text-red-600">\par
          <li><strong>Legalism:</strong> Treating giving as a requirement for salvation.</li>\par
          <li><strong>Manipulation:</strong> Promising guaranteed wealth in exchange for giving.</li>\par
          <li><strong>Cynicism:</strong> Refusing to give because of past leadership abuses.</li>\par
        </ul>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">DISCUSSION QUESTIONS</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>Do I give intentionally or impulsively based on emotion?</li>\par
          <li>How does the "Spirit-led" standard of the New Covenant challenge my current giving habits?</li>\par
          <li>In what ways can I support global missions through my local church?</li>\par
        </ul>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">WEEKLY ASSIGNMENT</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>Set aside a specific "Kingdom portion" of your next income before paying other bills.</li>\par
          <li>Find a need in your community and meet it anonymously this week.</li>\par
          <li>Memorize 2 Corinthians 9:7.</li>\par
        </ul>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">CONCLUSION</p>\par
        <p>Generosity is not about pressure; it\rquote s about gratitude. When the heart belongs to God, the wallet follows. We give because Christ gave Himself for us first (2 Corinthians 8:9).</p>\par
      </div>\par
    )\par
  \},\par
\par
\par
