\{ \par
    id: 24, \par
    title: "Lesson 24: Career & Marketplace Discipleship", \par
    description: "Bridging the gap between Sunday worship and Monday's work through excellence, skill development, and ethical leadership.",\par
    content: (\par
      <div className="space-y-2">\par
        <p className="font-bold">INTRODUCTION</p>\par
        <p>Discipleship that only works in church is incomplete. The marketplace is where your integrity is truly tested. Whether you are in a boardroom, a hospital, or managing properties, your work is your assignment. As Genesis 2:15 shows, work predates the fall\emdash it is a form of stewardship, not a punishment.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-4 text-lg">PART I: PURPOSE VS. PROFESSION</p>\par
        <p>It is vital to distinguish between these two:\par
          <ul className="list-disc ml-5 text-sm">\par
            <li><strong>Purpose:</strong> Eternal and unchanging. It is rooted in glorifying God (Ephesians 2:10).</li>\par
            <li><strong>Profession:</strong> Seasonal and practical. It is the vehicle (doctor, developer, manager) through which your purpose is expressed.</li>\par
          </ul>\par
          To find your path, assess your <strong>Gifts</strong> (natural abilities), your <strong>Burden</strong> (problems that move you), and your <strong>Capacity</strong> (skills and market demand).\par
        </p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-4 text-lg">PART II: SKILL & EXCELLENCE</p>\par
        <p>Skill is spiritual. Daniel distinguished himself because an "excellent spirit" was in him (Daniel 6:3). Anointing without competence limits your impact. \par
          <ul className="list-disc ml-5 text-sm">\par
            <li><strong>Continuous Learning:</strong> Commit to reading, certifications, and learning new technologies. If you stop learning, you lose relevance.</li>\par
            <li><strong>Work as Worship:</strong> Colossians 3:23 reminds us that while a supervisor signs the check, God evaluates the effort. Avoiding mediocrity is a kingdom mandate.</li>\par
          </ul>\par
        </p>\par
\par
        \par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-4 text-lg">PART III: TIME & RELATIONSHIPS</p>\par
        <p>Time mismanagement is hidden self-sabotage. Disciples must "make the most of every opportunity" (Ephesians 5:15-16). This includes planning objectives and guarding against burnout through Sabbath rest.</p>\par
        <p className="font-semibold pt-2">Workplace Witness:</p>\par
        <p>You don't need to be "weird" to be a witness. Influence grows through credibility, kindness, and moral courage. Address conflicts directly and avoid the trap of office gossip.</p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-4 text-lg">PART IV: LEADERSHIP & INTEGRITY</p>\par
        <p>Leadership is influence, not just a title. Following the model of Jesus (Mark 10:45), marketplace leaders should:\par
          <ul className="list-disc ml-5 text-sm">\par
            <li>Develop others and share knowledge.</li>\par
            <li>Make transparent, ethical decisions.</li>\par
            <li>Take initiative to solve problems before being asked.</li>\par
          </ul>\par
        </p>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">DISCUSSION QUESTIONS</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>Am I currently pursuing a career for prestige or to fulfill a kingdom purpose?</li>\par
          <li>In what specific professional skill do I need to improve this year to maintain excellence?</li>\par
          <li>Do my coworkers see the character of Christ in how I handle deadlines and stress?</li>\par
        </ul>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">WEEKLY ASSIGNMENT</p>\par
        <ul className="list-disc ml-5">\par
          <li>Perform a "Competence Audit": Identify one technical or soft skill to upgrade this month.</li>\par
          <li>Identify one person at work you can encourage or mentor this week.</li>\par
          <li>Memorize Colossians 3:23.</li>\par
        </ul>\par
\par
        <p className="font-bold pt-2">CONCLUSION</p>\par
        <p>The marketplace is your altar. When believers excel in their professions with unshakeable integrity, society shifts. Let your work preach, let your excellence speak, and let your conduct glorify God.</p>\par
      </div>\par
    )\par
  \},\par
\par
\par
\par
\par
